 be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{1-0}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with the implicit Euler method. In general, $Δy$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Δy & ={y}_{\\text{new}}^{′}\\cdot Δx \\\\  & =({e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+{y}_{\\text{new}})\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe substitute this into ${y}_{\\text{new}}=y+Δy$ and solve for the general formula for ${y}_{\\text{new}}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}+\\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now proceed to calculate our approximations of $y(\\frac{1}{2})$ and $y(1).$\n\n**Step 1**.\n\nFrom the initial conditions, we have\n\n$$\nx=0,\\,y=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=0+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\  & =2\\cdot 1+{e}^{1/2} \\\\  & ≈3.648\\,721,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\n**Step 2**.\n\nFrom the previous step, we have\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2},\\,y≈3.648\\,721.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the new $x$ value is \n\n$$\n{x}_{\\text{new}}=x+Δx=\\frac{1}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nHence, the new $y$ value is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{\\text{new}} & =2y+{e}^{{x}_{\\text{new}}} \\\\  & ≈2\\cdot 3.648\\,721+{e}^{1} \\\\  & ≈10.015\\,724,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to $6$ decimal places.\n\nTherefore, rounded to $2$ decimal places, we conclude that \n\n$$\ny(\\frac{1}{2})≈3.65,\\,y(1)≈10.02.\n$$" 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186314845 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314429 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186314845 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314535 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186314845 1069 "q-339732" 13194139533417 17592186045585 