articular, for $n=2,$ we have\n\n$$\nL{{t}^{2}f(t)}={F}^{″}(s).\n$$\n\nWe have that\n\n$$\nf(t)=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(-6t)=-\\operatorname{sinh}⁡6t.\n$$\n\nUsing the given result with $\\omega =6,$ the Laplace transform of $\\operatorname{sinh}⁡6t$ is $\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-36},$ so\n\n$$\nF(s)=-\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-36},\\,s>6.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating with respect to $s,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{′}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(-\\frac{6}{{s}^{2}-36}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(6({s}^{2}-36)^{-1}) \\\\  & =-(-6({s}^{2}-36)^{-2}\\cdot 2s) \\\\  & =\\frac{12s}{({s}^{2}-36)^{2}} \\\\ {F}^{″}(s) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{12s}{({s}^{2}-36)^{2}}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}s}(\\frac{s}{({s}^{2}-36)^{2}}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\frac{(s)^{′}\\cdot ({s}^{2}-36)^{2}-s\\cdot {(({s}^{2}-36)^{2})}^{′}}{({s}^{2}-36)^{4}}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}-36)^{2}-s\\cdot 2({s}^{2}-36)\\cdot 2s}{({s}^{2}-36)^{4}}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\frac{({s}^{2}-36)^{2}-4{s}^{2}({s}^{2}-36)}{({s}^{2}-36)^{4}}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\frac{{s}^{2}-36-4{s}^{2}}{({s}^{2}-36)^{3}}) \\\\  & =12\\cdot (\\frac{-3{s}^{2}-36}{({s}^{2}-36)^{3}}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{36{s}^{2}+432}{({s}^{2}-36)^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we used the quotient rule to find ${F}^{″}(s).$\n\nTherefore, by the smoothness property,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L{{t}^{2}\\operatorname{sinh}⁡(-6t)}={F}^{″}(s)=-\\frac{36{s}^{2}+432}{({s}^{2}-36)^{3}},\\,s>6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186315073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314063 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186315073 1068 #edb/ref 17592186314454 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186315073 1069 "q-341223" 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186315073 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 13194139533417 17592186045585 true] [17592186315073 1071 "Given that $y=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(x)),$ we have\n\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$\n{{field-1}}$\\cdot \\operatorname{s